            <ArticleTitle>[An important cause of shoulder-pain: the &quot;incisura scapulae syndrome&quot; (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>644-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Analysis of 124 of the author's cases shows that an isolated mechanical compression of the suprascapular nerve lies often at the bottom of shoulder pain without obvious cause. The term &quot;incisura scapulae syndrome&quot; is recommended. Causes, symptoms, diagnosis and treatment of this tunnel-syndrome are described in detail.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
